From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fixture Developer <dev@mobimanual.local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Keep queued commands for three days

Devices that are switched off over the weekend came back on Monday to find
their commands expired, and the helpdesk had to retry each one by hand.
Queued commands now stay valid for 72 hours before they expire.
---
Expected: worth documenting. Triage answers doc-impact, although the diff is one constant in server/. The draft changes the expiry from 24 to 72 hours on both pages that state it: _devices_id.md ("not acknowledged within 24 hours") and _devicescommands.md ("within 24 hours expires"). A draft that edits only one of them is incomplete. tr and de are translation debt.
Expected-outcome: opened
Expected-edits: _devices_id.md _devicescommands.md

 server/commands/command-queue.js | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/commands/command-queue.js b/server/commands/command-queue.js
index 1cf5b0d..9935300 100644
--- a/server/commands/command-queue.js
+++ b/server/commands/command-queue.js
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 // device has not acknowledged in time is marked expired; the console can queue
 // it again (Retry).
 
-const EXPIRY_HOURS = 24;
+const EXPIRY_HOURS = 72;
 
 function enqueue(db, deviceId, command, sentBy, now) {
   return db.commands.insert({
